    "faq": {
      "question_1": "What is the difference between an exposed and a concealed tap?",
      "answer_1": "An exposed tap is visible on the basin or wall. A concealed tap has its mechanism inside the wall, with the spout and controls visible. Always check which concealed body is required and whether it is included.",
      "question_2": "Which tap suits a countertop basin?",
      "answer_2": "A countertop basin needs enough height and reach between the spout and the bowl. A tall deck-mounted tap or a correctly positioned wall-mounted tap may suit it. Compare the tap dimensions with the height and position of your basin.",
      "question_3": "Are the concealed body and other parts included?",
      "answer_3": "This varies by product. A trim set is not automatically a complete tap. Check the product description and included components. Contact us if you are unsure whether you have everything needed for installation."
    },
